=============(Docker Compose)============
* is basically a tool that allows us to define and run multiple services
  and applications that belong together in one environment (1 isolated 
  environment)
* for building and running multi-container applications
* Docker compose which is built on top of docker engine it makes it incredibly
  easy to start applications with multiple containers



=========(Running multi-container Apps)=========
* Front-end : react
* Back-end  : node
* Database  : mongodb
* for running our front-end and back-end tests we need two terminal
  and also download and install mongodb
  ==> with docker we don't have to do any of these things all we have
      to do is run a single command 

* with docker file we have a YAML File:
  --> we use it to configure and maintain our application's services.
  --> with a single command, we create and start all the services from 
      our configuration
* compose.yaml structure :
  version: "3.1" ==> version of docker-compose
  services: == > list of all conatiners that we want to run 
    frontend: ==> container-name
    backend:
    mongodb:
      image: mongo
      ports:
        - 27017:27017
      environment:
        -MONGO..._USERNAME=admin
        -MONGO..._PASSWORD=secret


====> why we use yml files:
      for configuration files 
====> json for exchanging data between multiple computers
      like a client and a server.

=======>* docker network : 
  * allows containers to communicate with each other and with 
  the external world, cmd: docker network create nameNetwork
  * by default Compose, sets up a single network for our app


======> difference betweem up/down and start/stop